& [FADL_F014] is post-read enforcement under a local file race
  + [observed] field and report input metadata was checked before fs read and body length was checked afterward but a file that grew or was replaced between path operations could still allocate beyond the declared ceiling before rejection
  + [risk] the semantic rejection result was fail-closed while the allocation behavior was not fully bounded by the signed file budget
  + [repair] open once inspect metadata on that handle then stream through take of ceiling plus one byte and reject before deserialization when the sentinel byte exists
  + [proof] the existing file-budget test now covers exact-ceiling success and ceiling-plus-one streaming refusal while the complete P0 acceptance harness remains green
  + [boundary] handle-bound reading improves local resource discipline and does not claim adversarial production denial-of-service resistance
  + [status] is closed

& [FADL_R002] is name-based loopback without peer-address attestation
  + [observed] provider admission accepts canonical 127.0.0.1 or localhost text but the retained report does not prove the resolved socket peer address
  + [containment] every P0 evidence run uses numeric 127.0.0.1 proxies and redirects are disabled and the observed EVO-X2 server listener is exactly 127.0.0.1 port 8081
  + [boundary] current evidence does not demonstrate a route escape but localhost text alone is weaker than resolved-peer attestation
  + [reentry] a production transport profile may require numeric loopback only or retain independently checked connected-peer evidence
  + [status] is open_nonblocking_P0_residual

