& [FADL_R006] is provider identity preflight without replayable fault evidence
  + [observed] run without explicit model contacts v1 models before CycleReport construction and an unreachable admitted loopback endpoint exits one with stderr while creating no report
  + [supplied_identity_observation] run with a one-space explicit model constructs an attention-cycle fault but self-verification rejects the invalid provider identity so exit is one and no report is published
  + [causal_boundary] model validation occurs in field_request before post_chat and the observation uses unavailable 127.0.0.1 port 9 so no provider inference is possible
  + [requirement_tension] FADL-011 says every run yields ordered replayable sanitized evidence and typed faults but current proof begins only after valid field and provider model identity are available
  + [containment] every retained successful provider trace has complete report lineage and callers can supply an already admitted explicit model identity to bypass discovery while transport faults after report construction remain typed
  + [boundary] stderr and nonzero exit are honest failure signals but are not a replayable CycleReport or signed preflight envelope
  + [reentry] preserve new source and SJS authority for exact provider-identity validation plus either a typed preflight envelope a report profile with unresolved model identity or an explicitly narrower run-admission contract
  + [status] is open_requirement_nonblocking_experimental_residual

& [FADL_R007] is non-exact CLI argument admission
